# How we work (Idle Party)

Source: the owner, who vibe-codes. Last sync: **2026-11-19**.
This is the only always-on rule. `00-locks`, `10-what-to-build`,
`30-done`, `play-words`, and `hero-draw` are the full record. Open them
when their description matches. If they disagree, this page wins.

**Now:** Do the job named this turn, including the related fixes that make it true. A roadmap or week batch already taken on stays that whole batch. Do not start an unrelated feature; name it in the handoff. Commit locally when the checks are green. Cloud handoff is a branch and a PR. Do not merge, do not push a `test-*` or `v*` tag, and do not upload an AAB unless the owner asks in that turn.

## Current owner decisions (2026-11-19) — always apply

- **No economy, price, reward, or save-format change** without the owner's yes in that turn. Display text may change; ids, save keys, and JSON fields never do.
- **Never weaken a test.** A changed test asserts the same or more. Enemy catalog is append-only. Camera taus stay 0.05 / 0.09. Keep DODGE, BLOCK, and PARRY floating text.
- **UI target:** Brick Inc. Idle Breaker-style layout, dusk palette from the "Skymning med hjältar" art (plum, amber, muted gold, browns). Small visible button faces, hit areas stay 44 / 48 dp. `typeScaleMax` stays 1.45 and no `FittedBox` shrinking of text.
- **Approved versions are frozen.** New findings go into the next round, not into an approved PR.
- **Merge gate:** even "merge and release" means a test APK from the PR first, the owner's phone verdict, then merge. Play upload only on the owner's explicit OK (prefers 100% rollout).
- **No paid tools** (no Aseprite or paid services) for agent tooling.
- **Never force-push.** Never uninstall `com.idleparty.app` or wipe saves; only `com.idleparty.app.test` may be uninstalled on an emulator.
- **Keep runs small:** one batch per run, commit and push when that batch is green, then stop and hand off. Long multi-batch runs get interrupted and lose work.

## Chase

Strangers on Play become players. The party walks the room, one reason to
come back tomorrow, one Ascend loop. Principles: `docs/GROWTH_MANDATE.md`.
